Phase C of android-handoever.md (D2, finding F2): the android cargo feature dies — adb_client + image become normal deps, all #[cfg(feature = "android")]/#[cfg(not(...))] removed (core lib.rs/config.rs/error.rs comment, server server.rs nest + routes/mod.rs + setup.rs both fallback arms incl the only explicit "android feature not enabled" error, cli mod.rs x3). ADR-023 precedent: this repo already removed its llama.cpp build-time feature matrix in favor of always-compile + runtime-detect (Docker/bollard is the same pattern). Evidence for the reversal (recorded in ADR-024 decision 1, rewritten in this commit): android was the ONLY feature in the workspace; featureless builds silently 404'd /v1/android/* (its own author asked "is it not implemented yet?"); the MCP tools needed a matching-build pair of harness image AND server (the "dual-build gotcha"); build.sh/build-signed.sh never gained the flag so non-Windows bundles could never include android.

'Compiled in' != 'works out of the box': the /android page's SDK-not-ready panel and `xpressclaw android doctor` own the runtime expectation. Rejected middle ground (keep the gate + loud 501 stubs): more machinery than compiling it in (all pure Rust, cost is binary size/build time only).

Consequences now true everywhere: /v1/android/status always returns JSON -> the frontend's content-type probe (layout rail + live view) now always detects android once the server is up; the rail shows on every build, with the not-ready panel doing the explaining. default_mcp_servers() includes the android MCP server unconditionally -> every agent gets android_* tools on every build (senior's intent: android is a tool like shell/filesystem; tools error clearly at call time with no device). The harness image already carried mcp_android.py unconditionally — the dual-build trap is gone.

ORDERING (D3): build.ps1 still passes --features android at this commit and WOULD FAIL cargo ("package does not have feature") — the next commit fixes it; do not check out this commit alone and run build.ps1.

Verified: cargo check --workspace (no flags — first ever default build compiling adb_client, clean on Windows), cargo test -p core 361 pass, grep sweep of crates/.github/*.toml for feature = "android" / --features android is empty.
